  "query_preview": "..High pressure largely remains in control across \nnorthern Arizona for the duration of the forecast period. As a \nresult, temperatures will remain fairly steady each day, around \nfairly seasonable values. \n\nA weak upper-level low moving ejecting off the Pacific into \nCalifornia will slightly increase the pressure gradient on Sunday. \nEasterly winds increase a bit, with some afternoon gusts around 15-\n25 mph. Otherwise, winds look to remain fairly light through the \nduration of the forecast period, primarily from the northeast \nthrough southeast.\n\nDry conditions look to prevail through the weekend and into much of \nthe coming week as well. However, with some lingering moisture in \nplace, a stray afternoon shower can not be totally ruled out on \nWednesday as a weak shortwave drops through the Four Corners. The \nmost likely area will be across the higher terrain of eastern \nArizona, however the chances remain fairly slim. Beyond that, the \nensemble guidance does really signal towards much of a chance of \nprecipitation until potentially the 8-12 day time frame.",
